  "config": {
    "_comment": "Colours: yellow = warning, red = near critical. Tyres show no colour while fine. Temperature (the air inside the tyre): yellow from tyreWarn (130 F), red from tyreHot (150 F), nothing for cold. Pressure against the car's target: blue 3 psi under, yellow 3 psi over, red 5 psi over (UNEVEN against the other side of the axle when the car sends no target). Boost against target (only while the target is over 0.2 bar): white while fine, red when 3 psi (0.21 bar) off for 0.75 s.4 psi). Low pressure fuel (engine running): yellow under 4 bar, red under 3. Fuel rail: yellow under 25 bar, red under 15. Gearbox oil: yellow from 110 C, red from 125. Outside: yellow at 3 C and below (ice). Range: yellow under 80 km, red under 40. Intercooler: air after it yellow from 50 C, red from 60 C; heat soak (after minus outside) yellow from 20 C (36 F), red from 30 C (54 F).",
    "dme": {
      "comment": "Read from the engine unit (DME, ecu 18) with UDS 0x22 over the kit's read-only link, only while the page shows; candidates are tried in order, the first plausible one wins (value = raw * factor + offset). The identifiers M Vitals reads (cauliflowermossgrape, MIT). boostTarget / boostActual: intake manifold pressure setpoint and actual, absolute kPa (the outside air pressure, baro, is subtracted). hpfp: fuel rail (high pressure) bar. lpfp: low pressure fuel bar. loadTarget / loadActual: requested and actual relative air charge %. egs: gearbox oil temperature from the gearbox unit (ecu 24), asked only while the car's basic data set has none. chargeBefore / intake: the charge air before the throttle (ahead of the B58's water-to-air intercooler) and in the plenum after it: the intercooler's drop and heat soak (after minus outside). The B58 has no temperature sensor in the intercooler's water circuit. Boost is intake MANIFOLD pressure (after the throttle): never the charge pipe (pressure before the throttle: PID 0x70 'boost pressure sensor A', DME 4205 IPLAD), which spikes when the throttle shuts on a lift or a shift (seen at 27 psi, Nov 13 2026). oilPressure / afr / timing: as Apex Cluster reads them, asked only while a small box shows one.",
      "ecu": 18,
      "baro": [
        {
          "did": "4201",
          "bytes": 2,
          "at": 0,
          "factor": 0.00390625,
          "offset": 0,
          "min": 50,
          "max": 115,
          "note": "IPUMG, ambient pressure, u16 x 0.0390625 hPa -> kPa. DME8FF_R (MG1 DME: B58 / B48 / B38, G series), the identifiers cauliflowermossgrape's Live Data reads (MIT)"
        },
        {
          "did": "F433",
          "bytes": 1,
          "at": 0,
          "factor": 1,
          "offset": 0,
          "min": 50,
          "max": 115,
          "note": "OBD PID 0x33 barometric pressure, kPa (101.3 when not available)"
        },
        {
          "obd": "33",
          "bytes": 1,
          "at": 0,
          "factor": 1,
          "offset": 0,
          "min": 50,
          "max": 115,
          "note": "OBD service 01 PID 0x33 (same as F433)"
        }
      ],
      "boostTarget": [
        {
          "did": "57DB",
          "bytes": 2,
          "at": 0,
          "factor": 0.00390625,
          "offset": 0,
          "min": 20,
          "max": 255,
          "note": "AVG_OF_PSSOL, intake manifold pressure setpoint (mean), absolute: hPa = raw * 0.0390625, DME8FF_R reference (EdiabasX SGBD docs). Not 4AB0 (S_LADEDRUCK): that is the charge pressure setpoint, before the throttle."
        }
      ],
      "boostActual": [
        {
          "did": "4A2D",
          "bytes": 2,
          "at": 0,
          "factor": 0.0078125,
          "offset": 0,
          "min": 20,
          "max": 500,
          "note": "DRUCK_ABS_SAUGROHR, intake manifold absolute pressure, measured: hPa = raw * 20 / 256 (0..5120 hPa), DME8FF_R reference (EdiabasX SGBD docs)"
        },
        {
          "did": "580B",
          "bytes": 2,
          "at": 0,
          "factor": 0.00390625,
          "offset": 0,
          "min": 20,
          "max": 255,
          "note": "IPSAU, intake manifold absolute pressure: hPa = raw * 10 / 256 (reads up to 2560 hPa, about 22 psi of boost), DME8FF_R reference (EdiabasX SGBD docs)"
        },
        {
          "did": "F487",
          "bytes": 2,
          "at": 1,
          "factor": 0.03125,
          "offset": 0,
          "min": 20,
          "max": 600,
          "note": "OBD PID 0x87 intake manifold absolute pressure sensor A, 1/32 kPa"
        },
        {
          "did": "F40B",
          "bytes": 1,
          "at": 0,
          "factor": 1,
          "offset": 0,
          "min": 20,
          "max": 255,
          "note": "OBD PID 0x0B intake manifold absolute pressure, kPa (max 255 = 1.5 bar boost)"
        },
        {
